WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.400
I want to take up in volume 4 and begin with June 13, 1901. If you want to put a heading

2
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:20.640
on this, it's no cross, no crown. After a long silence on the part of my adorable Jesus,

3
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.960
at the most a few things about the scourges he wants to pour. This morning, as I was

4
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:33.920
oppressed and tired because of my hard position, especially because of the continuous privations

5
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:40.840
to which I am often subjected, I saw Jesus for short instances, and he told me, "My

6
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:48.960
daughter, crosses and tribulations are the bread of eternal beatitude." In other words,

7
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:57.000
you can decide yourself what height you want in heaven by the crosses and tribulations

8
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:05.800
that you accept from the Lord. I understood, Louisa said, that as we suffer more, more

9
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:11.640
abundant and more enjoyable will be the bread that will nourish us in the celestial dwelling,

10
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:18.360
so no cross, no crown. It's actually that simple. And the bigger the cross, the bigger

11
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:25.240
the crown. If you're size 10 on earth, you get a size 10 cross and you get a size 10

12
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:34.960
crown. If you are size 20 on earth, you get a size 20 crown. Now a size 20 crown doesn't

13
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:41.520
fit a size 10 head. So you get the crown that actually suits you that you've actually worked

14
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:51.920
towards. So the greater the deposit we receive in the future glory. So in Romans 8, Paul

15
00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.960
tells us that what God gives us in eternal glory is out of all proportion to anything

16
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:06.240
that we can suffer in this life. Also in 2 Corinthians 5, I think it is, St. Paul says

17
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:13.120
that we actually work on earth to make our own dwelling in heaven. And you can make it

18
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.160
with wood or straw, or you can make it with silver and gold, you can make a hot or you

19
00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:24.840
can make a palace, depending on your own decision.

20
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:33.000
So June 18, 1901, I have a VIP on this one. And this is that we are obliged to give glory

21
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:40.800
to God in everything we are.

22
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.720
As I was in my usual state, I saw my sweet Jesus for a little, and I began my laments

23
00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:53.120
about my poor state of his privations and about a sort of tiredness, both physical and

24
00:02:53.120 --> 00:03:02.320
moral, as if I felt my poor nature crushed. Now if the Lord doesn't actually sustain

25
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:08.280
her, she cannot stay alive because her life is absolutely abnormal.

26
00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.600
So as if I felt my poor nature being crushed and failing me in all its parts, and then

27
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:19.280
after I said all of this to Jesus, he told me, "My daughter, don't be concerned about

28
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:26.640
your feeling you're falling apart. I mean, it's incredible. Don't you know that everything

29
00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:32.680
must be sacrificed for me, not only in the soul, but also in the body?" So now we have

30
00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:39.520
a new picture for Louisa. She is a living sacrifice of praise and thanksgiving to God,

31
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.840
a daily sacrifice of praise.

32
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.720
And Jesus continued, "And that from the tiniest little particles of your being, I demand

33
00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:56.480
my glory. And then don't you know that from the state of union one passes on to another

34
00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:04.960
state that of consummation, two Thessalonians, one, twelve." So the state of union is like

35
00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:11.040
we get married and the state of consummation is that the marriage is consummated in this

36
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.520
oneness of the two.

37
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.640
So the state of consummation is a higher state than just the state of union. It's true that

38
00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:29.040
I'm not coming as usual so as to chastise the people.

39
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:35.980
But I use this also for your own prophet, which is not only that of keeping you united

40
00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:44.420
to me, but of consuming you for love of me. Now, it's only volume four and Louisa still

41
00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:53.040
doesn't understand that the privation of Jesus is a very big part of her sacrifice.

42
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.920
She doesn't accept it all that well and every now and then she's able to offer it out of

43
00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:05.560
love for him. But most of the time she just suffers it.

44
00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.520
After all Jesus said, "Do you not have great reason? You do not have great reason to afflict

45
00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:16.120
yourself. First, because when you see me, it's always from your interior that you see

46
00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:20.640
me. And this is the sure sign that I am with you.

47
00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:27.560
And also because not one day has yet come in which you can say that you have not seen

48
00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:34.040
me perfectly." Now, that is an absolutely extraordinary statement of Jesus. No other

49
00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:40.140
saint apart from our blessed mother could say that.

50
00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:46.560
After this Jesus' voice assumed a sweeter and more benign tone and he added, "My daughter,

51
00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:53.680
I recommend to you very, very much that you let not even the slightest act which is not

52
00:05:53.680 --> 00:06:00.600
patience, resignation, sweetness, sameness." That's the firmness, the immutability he's

53
00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:06.040
talking about, tranquility, and everything come out of yourself. Now, this applies most

54
00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:12.960
particularly to the time of the privations when she goes into a complete crisis. Otherwise,

55
00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:23.320
he said, "You would dishonor me." So he's demanding complete heroism from her.

56
00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:30.600
In these early volumes, it looks as if that heroism is almost impossible. But when you

57
00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:38.840
get up beyond volume 20, it's perfectly normal for her. So he is working on her bit by bit.

58
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:48.360
That is Philippians 1, 6. The work I have begun in you, I will complete." And he does

59
00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:57.800
complete this work in her in a very wonderful way. So he said, "Don't let anything that's

60
00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.080
not patience or resignation or sweetness and so on come out of you. Otherwise, you would

61
00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:08.800
dishonor me." And it would be the same as it would happen to a king who lived in a palace

62
00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:14.360
which was well adorned inside, but on the outside it could be seen full of cracks stained

63
00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:20.720
and about to collapse. Would people not say, "What? A king lives in this place?" And

64
00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:25.480
yet such an ugly configuration can be seen on the outside as to make one fear even to

65
00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:32.000
draw near it. Now, what Jesus is saying is, "Our faults, which are obvious to other

66
00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:40.960
people, are real blocks to them accepting the fact that God is working in us." Even

67
00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:47.200
Matthew Ghande is famous for having said that he loved Christ, but he couldn't bear Christians.

68
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:56.520
He said, "Now one of them is like him." And so we can really put people off. So Jesus

69
00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:03.080
continues, who knows what a king, oh yeah, who knows what a king he must be like. Would

70
00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:09.120
this not be a dishonor to the king? Now think that if anything which is not virtue comes

71
00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:15.920
out of view, they, that is everybody else, would say the same about me. And it would

72
00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:20.840
also dishonor the Lord because if the Lord puts up with anything, then the moral standards

73
00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:26.440
go down. As we see in the church today, because the priests are not holding up a high moral

74
00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:35.080
standard. And I who live inside of you would remain dishonored, Jesus said. So June the

75
00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:42.000
30th 1901, these are signs by which you will know that you have grace, therefore put a

76
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:49.960
VIP on this one as well. Louisa said, "As I was in my usual state, my most sweet Jesus

77
00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:57.320
made himself seen for a short time, all transfused in me. Now my book has a capital M there and

78
00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:03.720
it should be a small M because he's talking about Louisa. And he told me, "My daughter,

79
00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:08.400
do you want to know what the signs are to know whether a soul possesses my grace?"

80
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:16.040
Now Jesus said in volume two, "I am grace." Okay. So whether we possess the presence of

81
00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:22.180
God or not. And Louisa said, "Lord, as your most holy goodness pleases." And he replied,

82
00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:27.520
"Well, the first sign." So put in number one here, is to see whether the soul possesses

83
00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:35.520
my grace, is that in anything that belongs to God, which she may hear or see externally,

84
00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:41.120
she feels a sweetness, a gentleness fully divine in her interior, which is not comparable

85
00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:47.920
to anything human or terrestrial. It's the same as to a mother who recognizes the fruit

86
00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:53.280
of her womb in the person of her son, even from his breath, his voice, and she delights

87
00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:59.840
with joy. Or as two intimate female friends, who in conversing together, manifest the

88
00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:06.280
same sentiments in clinicians' joys, afflictions to each other. And since each one finds her

89
00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:12.460
own things engraved in the other, they feel such pleasure in them, such joy, and take

90
00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:18.600
them to heart so much that they cannot detach themselves. In the same way, the interior

91
00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:27.380
grace which resides in the soul on seeing externally the fruit of her womb, that is

92
00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:33.320
unrecognizing herself in those things which form her very existence, corresponds with

93
00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:38.320
them and makes the soul experience such joy and sweetness that one is unable to express

94
00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:46.720
it. Now, the examples that Jesus gives here are very interesting. First of all, to recognize

95
00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:54.280
that you're in the state of grace, many people are not sufficiently recollected or attentive

96
00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:58.520
to really know how they're feeling as to whether it would be grace or not. That would take

97
00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:04.000
a great deal of recollection. But it would be normal for someone like Louisa who's sitting

98
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:10.160
there in the bed giving all her attention to the Lord. And then the first example he

99
00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:18.420
gives is of a mother recognizing even the breath or smell or anything of her child.

100
00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:23.160
And then he gives an example that you're not expecting, and that is two intimate female

101
00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:30.280
friends. Now, one of the things that you find when you look at the history of the church

102
00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:36.880
is that saints don't come by themselves, saints usually come in clusters. And we have

103
00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:43.320
some amazing, let me call them couples, but I don't mean that sexually, I mean that the

104
00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:49.600
friendship is between a man and a woman, and they spur one another on to sanctity. If you

105
00:11:49.600 --> 00:12:02.320
take Francis and Clare in the 11th century, if you take Francis de Sales and Jane de Chantal,

106
00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:07.800
just to give you two examples out of many, it's usually that what Jesus here is giving

107
00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:14.040
friendship between two women. Friendship between two women can actually be very deep and they

108
00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:21.920
can be very, very close spiritually. And if you find such a friend, it is an amazing

109
00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:28.720
grace. And you should really appreciate it because they both of them spur each other

110
00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:37.600
on to sanctity. So the second sign that Jesus speaks about is that the words of the soul

111
00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:45.520
who possess grace are peaceful and they have the effect of casting peace into others. Now,

112
00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:55.000
you see, the God of peace is the God of grace, same person. So Jesus gives the sign of peace

113
00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:01.720
so very often as the sign of his presence. He is the prince of peace. He brings peace.

114
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:08.600
He only operates within us in peace. And when the grace is deep within us, put Philippians

115
00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:14.520
for seven that we have the peace that passes all understanding and guards our hearts and

116
00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:26.640
our minds in Christ Jesus. So if the person claiming to be living in grace doesn't show

117
00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:32.760
that there is peace inside of them and manifest peace to others, then you know that their claim

118
00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:39.920
isn't true. And Jesus said so much so that the same thing said by one who does not possess

119
00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:45.280
grace, make no impression and they bring no peace. While if they're said by the other

120
00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:51.480
one who possesses grace, they operate in a marvelous way and bring peace back to others.

121
00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:57.280
I remember hearing a priest speak about a retreat, a priest's retreat in Rome some years

122
00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:05.760
ago. And Mother Trees of Calcutta was invited to speak to them. And she came out on the

123
00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:14.000
stage and she spoke for approximately five, maybe seven or eight minutes. And he said

124
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:20.960
she didn't say anything that any the rest of us couldn't say. But he said the only person

125
00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:27.520
in the entire retreat that left a lasting impression was herself. And here you have

126
00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:35.540
the effect of somebody speaking from a very deep personal relationship with God and communicating

127
00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:41.080
that grace and peace to others. So what she was communicating wasn't just her words. She

128
00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:46.740
was communicating the presence and glory and peace of God to them. And I remember this

129
00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:53.040
priest was telling me this about six months later. And he said the impression she made

130
00:14:53.040 --> 00:15:01.040
on them was very profound. So we come to the next paragraph. Moreover Jesus said, grace

131
00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:10.320
strips the soul of everything and makes of her humanity a veil in which to remain covered.

132
00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:17.560
So that means that grace means that God is hidden in us in our humanity. And it's a bit

133
00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:28.640
like the the bread that is the external part of the consecrated host and it's hiding the

134
00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:38.920
presence of Jesus in the Eucharist. So a person in grace becomes a living host. Okay. So let

135
00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:43.280
me read it again. Grace strips the soul of everything. That is everything that is not

136
00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:51.000
of God and makes of her humanity a veil with which to remain covered in such a way that

137
00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:58.760
as the veil is torn, one finds paradise in the soul who possesses her. So it's no wonder

138
00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:05.200
that true humility, obedience and the like are found in that soul because there's nothing

139
00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:12.400
left of her. That means the earthy muddy stuff. There's nothing left of her but a simple

140
00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:20.920
veil. And one can see with clarity how it is all grace that acts within her and keeps

141
00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:28.080
all the virtues in order for her and make her remain in continuous attitude towards God.

142
00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:34.760
So Jesus is describing a soul that's completely open to God all the time and open to the

143
00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:43.480
imporings of God's presence in God's grace. It's a very good description of Louisa herself.

144
00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:53.240
So July the 5th 1901, Jesus is the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end. As I

145
00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:57.840
was concerned about the state of my soul, all of a sudden my adorable Jesus came and said

146
00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:04.840
to me, my daughter do not be concerned for I alone am the beginning, the means and the

147
00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:12.600
end of all your desires. With these words, I camped myself in Jesus. May everything be

148
00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:22.960
for the glory of God. So I want to give you John 14, 6, Revelation 1, 8 and Revelation

149
00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:36.320
21, 6. So we come to July the 16th 1901. The beginning of evil in man is the distance

150
00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:46.120
between the love of Jesus and human love. After various days of privation, this morning

151
00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:53.040
Jesus dained to come transporting me outside of myself. Now as I was present to him, I

152
00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:59.520
could see many people and the evil of the present generation. So that's Amos 3, 7 and

153
00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:08.160
Isaiah 64, 10. The Lord always tells his prophets first. So it's when Louisa goes into an outer

154
00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:20.160
body experience, there she sees clearly and she sees what God sees and she comes back

155
00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:27.800
with this prophetic message because as Jeremiah, when he spoke to one of the false prophets

156
00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:34.600
said, have you been in the Council of God? So these outer body experiences mean that

157
00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:45.360
Louisa is in the Council of God. And that's a huge thing if you know your Old Testament.

158
00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:51.320
And in the Council of God, God reveals what is happening on the earth to the person who

159
00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:59.240
is present to him. And as far as Jeremiah, the prophet is concerned, that is the sign

160
00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:10.040
of authenticity of a prophet that you've been in the presence of God. So Louisa said,

161
00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.800
when I was in the presence of blessed Jesus, I could see many people and the evil of the

162
00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:22.280
present generation. So that's pre World War one. And of course that evil is the communism

163
00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:31.320
and Marxist, atheism and materialism and rationalism and humanism and modernism and everything that

164
00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:39.160
was condemned by Popiah's intent. My adorable Jesus looked at them with compassion and

165
00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:48.080
turned to me and he said, my daughter, do you want to know where the evil of man began?

166
00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:54.680
The beginning of it is as soon as he knows himself. That is, as soon as he begins to

167
00:19:54.680 --> 00:20:03.680
acquire reason, man says to himself, I am something. I am an important person. Now this

168
00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:12.160
is very important and we'll explain to you why Jesus asks of us in the divine will spirituality

169
00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:18.920
to accept our nothingness, which is way beyond humility and to place our nothingness at

170
00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:25.640
his disposal, because it's only from that nothing that he can truly work. If you think

171
00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:33.600
of Blessed Mother's Magnificat in Luke chapter one, she said that the Almighty had regard

172
00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:39.600
for his lowly maiden. Now she was the most blessed of all creatures and if anybody could

173
00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:46.440
be tempted to call herself somebody, it was her. But this reminds me of a story, not a

174
00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:54.960
story of an incident that happened to me during my teaching years in Africa. I was doing a

175
00:20:54.960 --> 00:21:00.960
religion class and for some reason we got around to asking the girls what would they like to

176
00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:08.000
become and they said various things and then one little girl at the back put her hand up

177
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:15.540
and she said, I want to become a very important somebody. And I said to her, you know, you've

178
00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:23.360
